From: nim-gtk2 native audit
Subject: [PATCH] textview: invalidate overwrite cursors only on realized windows

GTK 2.24.33 can invalidate block cursors with a NULL layout and/or NULL GdkWindow
when overwrite changes on an unrealized TextView. Gate both invalidations on
realization; normal realization creates the layout/windows using the existing
native path and applies overwrite mode. No state is synthesized or realized early.

Optional GTK SOURCE patch only; the SDK never applies this or changes installed
libraries. Rebuild GTK separately if desired. Reproducer:
tests/headers/textview_overwrite.c with G_DEBUG=fatal-warnings.

--- a/gtk/gtktextview.c
+++ b/gtk/gtktextview.c
@@ -5864,7 +5864,8 @@
 static void
 gtk_text_view_toggle_overwrite (GtkTextView *text_view)
 {
-  if (text_view->text_window)
+  if (text_view->text_window &&
+      gtk_widget_get_realized (GTK_WIDGET (text_view)))
     text_window_invalidate_cursors (text_view->text_window);
 
   text_view->overwrite_mode = !text_view->overwrite_mode;
@@ -5873,7 +5874,8 @@
     gtk_text_layout_set_overwrite_mode (text_view->layout,
 					text_view->overwrite_mode && text_view->editable);
 
-  if (text_view->text_window)
+  if (text_view->text_window &&
+      gtk_widget_get_realized (GTK_WIDGET (text_view)))
     text_window_invalidate_cursors (text_view->text_window);
 
   gtk_text_view_pend_cursor_blink (text_view);
